==English==

===Etymology===
[[Norman]] baronial surname from a place in Normandy, {{etyl|fro}} ''Perci'' , Late {{etyl|la}} ''Persiacum'', from the Gallo-Roman personal name ''[[Persius]]''.

===Pronunciation===
* {{rhymes|ɜː(r)si}}

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun}}

# {{surname|A=An|English|from=Old French}}
# {{given name|male|from=surnames}}, transferred use of the surname since the Middle Ages.

====Usage notes====
*Also used as a pet form of [[Piers]] and [[Percival]].

====Quotations====
* '''~1597''' William Shakespeare: ''First Part of King Henry the Fourth: Act V, Scene IV'':
*: ''Hotspur''. My name is Harry '''Percy'''.
*: ''Prince''. Why, then, I see / A very valiant rebel of that name. / I am the Prince of Wales; and think not, '''Percy''', / To share with me in glory any more.
* '''2008''' [[w:Sebastian Barry|Sebastian Barry]], ''The Secret Scripture'', Faber and Faber, ISBN 978-0-571-21528-7, pages 198 - 199:
*: I have written again to ask if I may visit there sometime soon, and talk to the administrator, who it turns out is an old acquaintance, a man called Percival Quinn, I think the only '''Percy''' I have heard of in the present era, let alone met. 

===Anagrams===
* [[crepy#English|crepy]], [[crêpy#English|crêpy]]

